span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n<\/table>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Reference Ranges\r\n(<\/span><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>E.L.I.S.A)<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><b><span\r\nlang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span\r\nlang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Negative\u00a0\r\n: &lt; = 0.90<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span\r\nlang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Equivocal\u00a0\r\n: 0.91 \u2013 1.10<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span\r\nlang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Positive\u00a0\r\n: &gt; = 1.11<\/span><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\r\n<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Method\/Technology\r\n:<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>E.L.I.S.A : Solid\r\nphase capture Enzyme immunoassay<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Interpretation :<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>HIV ELISA is a\r\nscreening test being performed following NABL recommendations and NACO\r\nguidelines. The kits utilize a mixture of recombinant proteins for detection of\r\nantibodies to all subtypes of hiv \u2013 1 and hiv -2 in human serum or plasma. A\r\npositive report does not confirm diagnosis of HIV infection at any point of\r\ntime and all positive cases should be confirmed by confirmatory test like\r\nwestern blot or PCR, similarly, a no- reactive test does not exclude the possibility\r\nof HIV infection and must be interpreted by a medical practitioner in light of\r\nthe exposure and possible window period.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Please corre